.Dd October 2, 2026
.Dt RESIZE2FS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm resize2fs
.Nd grow or shrink an ext2 file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fFpPMbs
.Op Fl d Ar debug-flags
.Op Fl S Ar RAID-stride
.Op Fl z Ar undo_file
.Ar device
.Op Ar size
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
grows or shrinks the ext2 file system on
.Ar device .
Rach2 uses e2fsprogs 1.47.4, built with the resizer enabled and linked
statically against the ported musl.
The program is installed in the recovery image and on the GNU system, at
.Pa /sbin/resize2fs .
The GNU system's ordinary kernel takes no write to a disk node, so there
it resizes a volume in a file or on a loop device.
.Pp
The volume must be unmounted.
Rach2 has no on-line resize support.
The recovery system mounts nothing from the disk it works on, and
.Nm
reads
.Pa /proc/mounts
to refuse a mounted volume.
.Pp
Run
.Ql e2fsck -f
before resizing.
Unless
.Fl f
is given,
.Nm
refuses to resize a volume not checked since its last mount.
.Pp
.Ar size
is the requested size in file system blocks.
Suffixes
.Ql K ,
.Ql M ,
.Ql G ,
and
.Ql T
specify powers-of-two kilobytes, megabytes, gigabytes, and terabytes;
.Ql s
specifies 512-byte sectors.
Without
.Ar size ,
the program uses the partition size reported by the kernel through
.Ql BLKGETSIZE64 .
The requested size must not exceed the partition.
.Pp
The partition nodes provide raw sector access.
As with
.Xr e2fsck 8 ,
the library uses whole-sector I/O and a bounce buffer for partial-sector
requests.
.Nm
keeps the volume's bitmaps in memory.
.Xr growroot 8
refuses to run it when
.Ql MemTotal
is less than 7 MiB.
.Pp
.Xr growroot 8
enlarges the partition, runs its two file system checks, and invokes
.Ql resize2fs DEVICE
to grow the file system to the partition size.
If an interrupted resize leaves errors, run
.Ql e2fsck -f -p
to repair the volume.
After repair, run
.Xr growroot 8
again to complete the resize.
The
.Ql rach2-install
installer uses growroot when the person agrees to grow the root.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b
Enable the 64bit feature, resize group descriptors, and move other
metadata as needed.
Changing the 64bit feature cannot be combined with resizing the file
system.
.It Fl d Ar debug-flags
Enable debugging features compiled into the program.
Add the desired values:
.Bl -tag -width 32 -compact
.It 2
Block relocations.
.It 4
Inode relocations.
.It 8
Inode table moves.
.It 16
Timing information.
.It 32
Minimum size calculation for
.Fl M .
.El
.It Fl f
Force the resize, overriding some safety checks.
.It Fl F
Flush the device's buffer cache before resizing; on Rach2 the flush
request answers
.Er ENOTTY
and the run ends before the resize.
.It Fl M
Shrink to the smallest size permitted by the stored files.
.It Fl p
Print percentage completion bars for each stage of an off-line resize.
Very fast operations may display no progress bar.
.It Fl P
Print an estimate of the size, in file system blocks, that
.Fl M
would produce, then exit without resizing.
.It Fl s
Disable the 64bit feature and free blocks no longer needed.
Changing the feature cannot be combined with resizing the file system.
.It Fl S Ar RAID-stride
Use the specified RAID stride instead of the value inferred from the
file system.
.It Fl z Ar undo_file
Save each block's old contents in an undo file before overwriting it.
An empty argument selects
.Pa resize2fs-device.e2undo ,
with
.Ql device
replaced by the device name, in the directory
.Ev E2FSPROGS_UNDO_DIR
names, or
.Pa /var/lib/e2fsprogs
when it is unset; a value that is empty or
.Ql none ,
or a directory that cannot be written, disables the undo file without a
word.
The undo file cannot recover from a power failure or system crash.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /sbin/resize2fs
.It Pa /sbin/resize2fs
The resizer of the recovery image and of the GNU system.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
returns 0 on success and a nonzero status on failure, with the reason
on standard error.
Growroot reports a failure as
.Ql resize2fs status N .
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the recovery system, check the unmounted root partition and grow
it to the partition size:
.Dl e2fsck -f /dev/disk0p3 && resize2fs /dev/disk0p3
.Pp
Growroot changes the partition table first, then checks and grows the
file system:
.Dl growroot MBRID=ID,3
.Pp
In the source tree,
.Ql tests/run grow
exercises a resize interrupted and completed by a second growroot run.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
A volume that needs checking before a resize produces:
.Dl Please run 'e2fsck -f DEVICE' first.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr disk 7 ,
.Xr recovery 7 ,
.Xr e2fsck 8 ,
.Xr growroot 8
